Zhorx AI Lead Response & Qualification (n8n Workflow)
This is an n8n workflow that handles new leads for you from start to finish. When someone fills out your form, it checks the lead, scores it with AI, saves it to HubSpot, sends a personal reply, pings your team on Slack, and follows up over the next few weeks until the lead books a call or replies.

What it does
Takes in new leads from your website form through a webhook.
Checks that the important fields are filled in. If something is missing, it flags the lead for review instead of losing it.
Uses AI to score the lead as HOT, WARM, or COLD and figure out their main problem and what service fits best.
Saves the contact and deal to HubSpot.
Writes and sends a short, personal email to the lead.
Sends a Slack alert for hot and warm leads so your team can jump on them.
Follows up automatically on day 2, 5, 10, and 20. It stops on its own once the lead books a meeting, replies, or is marked done.
Watches your Google Calendar and Gmail so it knows when a lead books or replies, then stops the follow-ups.
Keeps lead data safe if anything breaks, so nothing gets dropped.
What you need
n8n (cloud or self-hosted)
Accounts connected for: OpenAI, HubSpot, Gmail, Slack, Google Calendar
A few custom HubSpot fields: zhorx_lead_score, zhorx_lead_temperature, zhorx_recommended_service, zhorx_monthly_leads, zhorx_automation_needed, zhorx_source, zhorx_lead_created_at, zhorx_meeting_time
How to use it
Import the .json file into n8n (Workflows, then Import from File).
Connect your accounts in each node.
Set your Slack channel, Google Calendar, and swap in your own wording.
Point your website form to the webhook URL.
Turn the workflow on.
